@title  PCSA00002 - take control of a team and PLAY: menu walk, then swing at the plate
@game   PCSA00002
@shot-every 400

# WHY THIS RECIPE EXISTS, AND WHY `swing-and-play` IS NOT IT
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# `swing-and-play` never swings, and nothing it presses at the plate reaches the game. Its
# menu walk is a blind run of `cross` presses that leaves TEAM SELECT with **Rangers CPU vs
# Cardinals CPU and P1 unassigned**, so the title has been playing itself in every run this
# project has taken - the ball is hit by a CPU batter, on the CPU's schedule, and our input
# is read by nobody. Its 16-point touch sweep across the title screen is fiction too: the
# title screen is dismissed by START, and sits there through the whole sweep.
#
# This one walks the menu that was actually walked and shot step by step, and the step that
# matters is `left` at TEAM SELECT: it moves P1 onto the ROAD team, who bat first. After
# that the batter is OURS and `cross` is the swing.
#
# Every step carries a `@shot`, so a run of this recipe says for itself whether the walk
# still lands - a menu that has moved shows up as a wrong picture at a named step rather
# than as a silent arrival somewhere else.

0: @section boot

1900: @section accept-user-settings
1900: cross
1910:
2200: @shot after-user-settings

3800: @section title-screen-start
3800: start
3810:
4100: @shot game-modes

4400: @section exhibition
# GAME MODES, with EXHIBITION already highlighted.
4400: cross
4410:
4700: @shot exhibition-modal

5000: @section play-now
# The EXHIBITION / PLAY NOW / CANCEL modal.
5000: cross
5010:
5300: @shot team-select

5600: @section take-the-road-team
# >>> THE STEP THE OLD RECIPE MISSED. `left` moves P1 from "unassigned" onto the ROAD team
# (Texas), who bat first - so the first at-bat is ours to swing at. `r` here would change
# the LEAGUE (MLB -> TRIPLE-A), not advance, which is the other way this screen was misread.
5600: left
5610:
5900: @shot p1-on-the-road-team
6000: cross
6010:
6300: @shot road-uniform

6600: @section uniform
6600: cross
6610:
6900: @shot select-pitcher

7200: @section pitcher
7200: cross
7210:
7500: @shot pregame-lineup

7800: @section lineup-press-start
# The PREGAME LINEUP screen says PRESS START, and `cross` does not leave it.
7800: start
7810:
8100: @shot stadium-select

8400: @section stadium
8400: cross
8410:
8700: @shot options

9000: @section options-confirm
9000: down
9010:
9060: down
9070:
9120: down
9130:
9180: cross
9190:
9600: @shot loading-into-the-game

10200: @shot in-the-game
10600: @shot at-the-plate

11000: @section swing
# >>> OURS TO SWING NOW. `cross` is the normal swing on this title; the CPU pitches on its
# own schedule and nothing here can see the pitch, so the swings walk a steady cadence
# across a long window rather than trying to time one. Missing costs a strike and another
# pitch; contact only has to happen once.
11000: cross
11003:
11060: cross
11063:
11120: cross
11123:
11180: cross
11183:
11240: cross
11243:
11300: cross
11303:
11360: cross
11363:
11420: cross
11423:
11480: cross
11483:
11540: cross
11543:
11600: cross
11603:
11660: cross
11663:
11720: cross
11723:
11780: cross
11783:
11840: cross
11843:
11900: cross
11903:
11960: cross
11963:
12020: cross
12023:
12080: cross
12083:
12140: cross
12143:

12300: @section play-it-out
# Nothing is pressed here: a ball in play is the FIELDERS' to resolve, and a button during
# it advances a prompt that has not appeared yet.
12400: @shot the-ball-is-in-play
13000: @shot after-the-play
